D7 -- unbounded ingest pagination.

Defect: app/core/data_processing.py:28, 'while True' whose only exits were a
falsy response from fetch_api_data and len(ests) < max_results. Neither fires if
the FSA enhanced-search endpoint returns a full page indefinitely, which is what
happens if it ignores the page segment of the URL
(api_client.py:22 puts page and max_results in the path, not the query string --
a malformed value degrades silently rather than erroring). In the Cloud Run cron
that is an unattended infinite loop with a 1s sleep and unbounded list growth.

Fix: 'for page in range(1, max_pages + 1)' with for/else. The else clause only
runs when the loop was not broken out of -- i.e. the cap was reached without a
short page -- which is exactly the ambiguous case worth warning about.

Default of 50 chosen as a runaway guard, not an expected limit: the FSA search
returns at most a few thousand establishments within the configured radius, and
production configs pass max_results=5000, so real runs break on page 1. Anything
tight enough to truncate a legitimate ingest would be worse than the bug.

Cap is per coordinate, asserted by test_page_cap_applies_per_coordinate -- a
shared counter would let one exhausted coordinate shorten the next one's fetch.

Verification: pytest app/ scripts/ -> 90 passed. Red phase: 3 failures
(TypeError on the unknown max_pages kwarg) before implementation.
